Source: grub-btrfs
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: SOS developers <sos@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/Antynea/grub-btrfs
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: grub-btrfs
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, bash, btrfs-progs, gawk, grub-common
Recommends: inotify-tools
Description: GRUB boot menu entries for btrfs snapshots
 Adds a "snapshots" submenu to GRUB so any snapper snapshot of the root
 subvolume can be booted. grub-btrfsd regenerates the menu when snapshots
 are created or deleted. In SOS this is "yesterday's system is one entry in
 the boot menu".
